    "lawCode": "Amd §2.10, CP L",
    "lawSection": "Criminal Procedure Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1149\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the criminal procedure law, in relation to designating\nuniformed court officers of the town of New Windsor as peace officers\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis bill designates uniformed town court officers in the Town of New\nWindsor as peace officers upon the certification of the Division of\nCriminal Justice Services, in consultation with the Municipal Police\nTraining Council, that such officers have received sufficient training\nto fulfill their duties and responsibilities in an adequate manner.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1: Amends Criminal Procedure Law section 2.10 by adding a new\nsubdivision 83 to designate such town court officers as peace\nofficers.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nUnder current law, such officers are not designated as peace officers.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis bill was requested by the Town of New Windsor Town Board. This\nbill was requested by the Town because the Office of Court\nAdministration believes that many town courts have a heightened need\nfor security personnel to protect court employees, litigants and the\ngeneral public. Further, there was an incident in the nearby Village\nof Sloatsburg Justice Court in which shots were fired, which nearly\nhit the presiding justice. The OCA, through JCAP grants, has been\nfunding metal detectors for town and village court rooms, but does not\nhave the money to fund the personnel needed to operate such machines.\nAuthorizing the Town of New Windsor to use peace officers for this\ntask would increase safety in this town's court room.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nA new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediate.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
